menu "EPSolar Zigbee sensor"

config EPSOLAR_UPDATE_INTERVAL_SECONDS
    int "Telemetry update interval (seconds)"
    range 1 86400
    default 60
    help
        Time between Modbus reads and Zigbee attribute updates.

config EPSOLAR_ZIGBEE_IDLE_POLL_MS
    int "Sleepy end device idle poll interval (milliseconds)"
    range 1000 60000
    default 5000
    help
        How often the node polls its parent between telemetry cycles. The
        library never leaves fast poll (espressif/esp-zigbee-sdk#782), so the
        fast poll interval is the idle wake rate, and this value - applied
        once each cycle's APS ack exchange has finished - is what the light
        sleep length comes from. Joining, rejoining and the ack exchange
        itself always run at the 200 ms library default instead: association
        and rejoin responses must be fetched within macResponseWaitTime,
        about 491 ms, and the parent discards an APS ack after
        macTransactionPersistenceTime, 7.68 s.

        The 5 s default sits below that 7.68 s persistence with margin: the
        parent holds any downlink frame - an unsolicited read, OTA, a
        Configure Reporting - long enough for the node's next poll to collect
        it, so downlink stays reliable. Push past 7.68 s and downlink frames start
        being discarded before a poll arrives. At any idle-length interval
        the rejoins the stack starts on its own after a parent link flap
        already miss the 491 ms deadline; the repair ladder recovers those by
        steering at 200 ms, but only after minutes of silence.

config EPSOLAR_REPORT_PACING_MS
    int "Gap between report transmissions (milliseconds)"
    range 0 1000
    default 50
    help
        Pause after each attribute write and each reporting-record arm during
        a telemetry cycle, with the Zigbee stack lock released so the
        mainloop transmits the report the write fired before the next one is
        queued. Zero paces nothing: the cycle's ~16 frames leave the radio
        back to back.

        The back-to-back burst is the sharpest load the node puts on its
        supply and is fatal on a supply that sags under it; paced single
        frames give the rail recovery time between transmissions, at the
        cost of under a second of extra awake time per cycle. Pacing also
        stops the publish path from draining the stack's fixed out-buffer
        pool faster than the mainloop refills it.

config EPSOLAR_LIGHT_SLEEP
    bool "Enable automatic light sleep"
    depends on PM_ENABLE && FREERTOS_USE_TICKLESS_IDLE
    default y
    help
        Sleep between telemetry cycles. The Zigbee stack and the Modbus
        transactions hold the chip awake whenever they need it, so this only
        covers genuinely idle time. The firmware checks for a USB host once
        at boot and keeps light sleep off for that whole run when one is
        present: USB Serial JTAG does not survive a light sleep, and the USJ
        connection monitor's own no-light-sleep lock is not reliable at
        1000 Hz ticks. Turn this off outright to force the same no-sleep
        reference behaviour on battery as well.

config EPSOLAR_MODBUS_UART_PORT
    int "Modbus UART port"
    range 0 1
    default 1
    help
        UART0 and UART1 are the ESP32-C6 high-performance UARTs. UART1 is
        used by default so USB Serial/JTAG remains available for logs.

config EPSOLAR_MODBUS_TX_GPIO
    int "Modbus UART TX GPIO"
    range 0 30
    default 16
    help
        XIAO D6, labelled TX.

config EPSOLAR_MODBUS_RX_GPIO
    int "Modbus UART RX GPIO"
    range 0 30
    default 17
    help
        XIAO D7, labelled RX.

config EPSOLAR_MODBUS_BAUD_RATE
    int "Modbus baud rate"
    range 1200 115200
    default 115200

config EPSOLAR_MODBUS_SLAVE_ADDRESS
    int "Modbus slave address"
    range 1 247
    default 1

endmenu
